WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:00.843
(people applauding)

00:00:00.843 --> 00:00:01.965
- Welcome to The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:00:01.965 --> 00:00:06.200
give it up for my band playing
Bad Habits by Ed Sheeran,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.033
Yeah.

00:00:08.597 --> 00:00:10.600
So we have someone on the line

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.830
who is very familiar with that song.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.404
Can we say hi to him, everybody?

00:00:15.404 --> 00:00:16.237
(band music)

00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:17.944
What's up Ed Sheeran!

00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:20.944
(audience cheering)

00:00:24.101 --> 00:00:26.354
Get it out, get it out people.

00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:28.220
They love you.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.830
It is great to see you again.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.450
I will, I'm gonna lead with this.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.620
It is absolutely terrifying
to be singing someone's song

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.631
and then listening.

00:00:35.631 --> 00:00:37.010
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.720
I was like, oh my God.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.640
I was like, it's terrible.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.160
I love that song though.
Bad habits is such a jam.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.320
I love it. Why did you write that?

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.153
- Ah, thank you.

00:00:45.153 --> 00:00:46.165
I loved your version by the way.

00:00:46.165 --> 00:00:48.180
I was listening to your version,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.810
wondering whether I
should have actually used

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.000
more electric guitar in it,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.349
'cause it sounded pretty great.

00:00:52.349 --> 00:00:53.360
(people laughing)

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.543
I wrote it,

00:00:56.309 --> 00:00:58.030
by accident.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.893
I was working with,

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.580
the two people that I've
made the album with Johnny,

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.410
Johnny and Fred and Fred is
primarily like a dance producer.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.530
And he played me a tune that
he was just about to release.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.280
It was a really, really heavy dance tune.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.240
And I just said, you know what?

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.240
Let's just try and make something upbeat

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.840
that could also be played on
acoustic guitar life basically.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.400
And yeah, it just kind
of happened by accident.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.930
I wasn't expecting it to be first single

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.150
and yeah it's one of these
songs that sort of came out

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.640
and it's just kind of stuck

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.430
and it's not like it's,

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:34.530
it hasn't been like my
biggest charting single,

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.012
but I think it'll end up being,

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:36.845
- Longevity

00:01:36.845 --> 00:01:38.180
- one of my biggest songs just over time,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.160
- Yeah that's longevity.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:39.993
- very very gradually.

00:01:39.993 --> 00:01:41.130
- And that's the best kind of song though.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.690
And also, I didn't want to freak you out,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.550
but my idea was actually
to completely do it

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.530
with just a piano,

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:47.630
and I wanted to make
it really dark and sad

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.090
and then I didn't want to freak you out.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.028
So I kept it like this,

00:01:50.028 --> 00:01:50.980
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.340
but I love a song like that.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.610
I feel like you write songs like that,

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.250
that you can literally
do with a huge band,

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.260
electric guitars, do it big.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.100
You could do dance, you
can do singer songwriter.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.710
I think it's an amazing
gift you have, songwriting.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.440
Everybody knows that but,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.600
so you were a mega mentor
on The Voice this season.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.600
Super stoked about that.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.901
But I have to ask who was
your favorite coach Ed?

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.510
(audience laughs)

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.310
I mean, who was it, just shout it out.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.245
Just don't feel shy.

00:02:14.245 --> 00:02:18.385
- Well Kelly, only one person,
only one person debut there.

00:02:18.385 --> 00:02:19.560
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.382
- No like, I can't say.

00:02:21.382 --> 00:02:22.730
- [Ed] It must've been
you because I still,

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.600
actually, I still have the jacket.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.998
- You still, see, I gave you presents.

00:02:25.998 --> 00:02:28.950
- I still have the jacket in this house.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.427
- I will buy your love
Ed Sheeran. I will do it.

00:02:32.427 --> 00:02:34.380
Well, no, your daughter Lyra,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.570
which is the most beautiful name ever.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.750
She just turned one.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.720
So how do you think we
were talking about her

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.690
whenever you were visiting?

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.870
'Cause it was your
first time away from her

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.030
for that amount of time.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.330
So how do you think she's changed you?

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.513
- Well, I mean, my
bedtime has shifted from,

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.640
I'm no longer going to bed at five.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.830
I'm getting up at four
or five, which is good,

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.850
but no, I think there's
like a different emotion

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.520
that has come through having a daughter.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.750
And man, she's just wonderful.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.850
She's just wonderful.
She's just started walking.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.900
She knows what her eyes and head and mouth

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:08.733
and blah, blah, blah.

00:03:08.733 --> 00:03:10.570
And she's on the verge
of talking and just,

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:13.410
it's incredible to watch
all these things happen.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.430
- [Kelly] It is so cool.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.790
It's so exciting how fast they change.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.020
Like every, it's such a cliche statement,

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.190
but they change so quickly, so fast.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.860
Well, your new album is called Equals.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.310
So what's this all about?
Other than being equal.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.983
- Well, no, the equal sign actually comes,

00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:28.530
I feel like being 30,

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.369
like equals is at the end of a question

00:03:31.369 --> 00:03:32.400
and the start of an answer.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.100
And I feel like my twenties were just

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.420
a hell of a lot of questions.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.190
And my thirties, now all those questions

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.750
are starting to get answered,

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.770
for better or for worse.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.100
And yeah, so the album is just,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.740
I'd say it's a quarter life crisis album,

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.900
but it's essentially like turning 30,

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.130
getting married, having a kid,

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.410
losing a friend and sort of figuring out

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.440
who I am around all of that.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.273
- Yeah. I love that.

00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:57.630
Well, a lot of people are
going to relate to that.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.790
I cannot wait to hear it.
We're all dying to hear it.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.870
You're touring again, which
I know a lot of artists,

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.487
you know, we're all
stoked to be doing again.

00:04:03.487 --> 00:04:05.156
(audience cheering)

00:04:05.156 --> 00:04:07.330
So where are you looking
forward to playing?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.300
Are you looking forward
to like hometown shows?

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.133
- Yeah. Do you know?

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.750
I'd never really do hometown shows until

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.583
the end of the tour.

00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:17.340
'Cause that sort of feels
like the time where you finish

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.980
and that's the celebration.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.100
So I'm looking forward,
I'm playing some cities

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.010
and islands that I've never played before.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.040
I always loved touring islands,

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:25.873
but to be honest,

00:04:25.873 --> 00:04:27.700
the first leg of the tour,

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.620
I'm doing the kind of places
where it's safe to do shows

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.590
at the moment in Europe,

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.230
where they've sort of had festivals

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.710
and it's tried and tested and
everything's COVID secure.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.610
'Cause I just want to see
if the tour works first

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.737
before bringing it elsewhere.

00:04:41.737 --> 00:04:43.330
So I'm excited to play London.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.190
I'm excited to play Paris.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:47.580
I'm excited to play all
the cities in Germany,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.720
but I will be coming
to the States in 2023.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.240
All the dates are getting finalized now

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.263
and its getting back out there.

00:04:52.263 --> 00:04:53.096
(audience cheering)

00:04:53.096 --> 00:04:56.140
- Don't you be a liar, you
better bring your show here

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.390
'cause I wanna go.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.370
It's nice to see you and thank you so much

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.540
for zooming in.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.220
- Kelly, can I just say,

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.990
can I just say it was such a wonderful day

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.060
hanging out with you on The Voice

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.000
and I just think you're
such a fabulous person,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.669
and I can't wait to see you soon.

00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:12.502
So thank you for having me back.

00:05:12.502 --> 00:05:16.404
- Well, thank you! Thank you,
see, the jacket did buy love.

00:05:16.404 --> 00:05:18.190
(audience clapping)

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.590
Once again Ed's new
album is called Equals,

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.290
be sure to check it out everybody.

